WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.880
SCP-096 versus SCP-3166. Who comes out&nbsp;
on top between the brutalizing Shy Guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.960
and the horrific, lasagna-filled&nbsp;
Garfield-creature? Let’s find out.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.080
SCP-3166 is a creature resembling a mascot&nbsp;
costume of the character Garfield that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.560
attacks critics of the franchise through severe&nbsp;
bodily harm or the force-feeding of lasagna.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.200
In a theoretical test between the two anomalies,&nbsp;
Garfield creator Jim Davis would accidentally see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:32.400
a tiny fraction of SCP-096’s visage. SCP-3166&nbsp;
would manifest to ensure that nothing happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:38.960
to the Garfield strip, potentially stopping 096&nbsp;
. On the other hand SCP-096 has the durability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.800
to withstand high-grade Foundation equipment,&nbsp;
with striking speed to match. SCP-3166 couldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.600
defend itself against such a fast and powerful&nbsp;
opponent, no matter how much lasagna it tried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.480
to shove down the Shy Guy’s throat. Sorry&nbsp;
Garfield, looks like it’s a Monday for you.

